\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Content and editing model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Jude is the site's sole editor for now. Izzy is not paying for a hosted CMS and does not edit the site herself.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Most site content (copy, services, pricing, testimonials) lives as structured, typed files in the repo (TS or JSON, MDX for longer copy), edited directly and redeployed. No hosted service, no runtime dependency.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The blog is the one area with a proper editing UI: a local, git-based CMS that Jude runs on his own machine.
\f1\b0  Recommended: 
\f0\b Keystatic in local mode
\f1\b0  (TinaCMS local mode is a fine alternative). The admin UI runs locally (e.g. at 
\f2\fs26 /keystatic
\f1\fs24 ), posts are authored through it, saved as MDX into the repo (e.g. 
\f2\fs26 /content/blog
\f1\fs24 ), committed to git, and deployed by Vercel. Free, no client subscription, no hosted auth. Scope the CMS config to the blog collection only, leave everything else as typed in-repo content.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

