\cf0 \strokec2 These colours can be rearranged if we want more pop here and there.\
Important: terracotta is a vivid, saturated orange, so use it sparingly. It's the warm punctuation (buttons, links, small accents), never a large fill. The site should read as soft whites and greens with terracotta as the occasional warm note. Lock all text/background pairings to WCAG AA contrast (watch mid green and terracotta on cream especially).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Typography (lean into "thin")\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Display / headings: an elegant light-weight serif (Cormorant Garamond is a great fit) at light or regular weight. Large, airy, delicate.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Body: a clean humanist sans at light/regular weight for readability (Inter, or a soft geometric like Jost).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Generous line height and letter spacing. Hairline weights, plenty of negative space. Nothing bold or heavy anywhere.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 "Brushed" texture direction\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is central to the look, so build it in properly rather than as an afterthought:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hand-painted brushstroke SVG shapes as section dividers and as soft backing behind headings.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Subtle ink-wash / watercolour texture accents in sage and green, low opacity.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hand-drawn style underlines or highlights on a few key words.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A very subtle grain/paper texture over cream sections so it feels tactile, not flat.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Buttons and cards with soft, slightly organic edges rather than hard rectangles.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Motion (Framer Motion)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Calm and slow. Gentle opacity and position reveals on scroll, soft easing, nothing bouncy or fast. Where it fits, a reveal that feels like a brushstroke wiping content in. Motion should soothe, not perform.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

