\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Google reviews (this is her strongest asset, get it right)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 She has 36+ Google reviews and they convert, so reviews should be prominent and trustworthy. Recommended hybrid approach:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Curated testimonials (primary):
\f1\b0  hand-pick her best reviews into a beautifully designed, on-brand testimonials section. Stored as structured content in the repo and updated by hand. Full design control, always looks great, no runtime dependency.\
\ls13\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Live aggregate rating (Google Places API):
\f1\b0  server-side fetch of her overall star rating and total review count via the Places API "Place Details" endpoint, cached (revalidate daily). Use this for the trust line ("4.9 from 36 reviews") and for schema. Note: Place Details only returns up to 5 reviews, so it's for the rating/count and an optional "latest" strip, not the full list.\
\ls13\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Link out to the full profile everywhere it matters.
